data.content:
**In .NET 11, all synchronous I/O on the EF Core Cosmos DB provider is fully removed — no opt-in can restore it.** Your .NET 10 `EnableSyncIO` workaround no longer works; every sync call will throw at runtime.

**What breaks:** `ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()`, and `SaveChanges()` — all four methods in your repository.

**Fix — convert to async:**

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

Callers of these methods will also need to be updated to `await` the results. This is the only path forward — the Cosmos SDK is async-only, and EF Core 11 no longer wraps it in sync-over-async.
